    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive setup, anchored by the premium matchups for **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Jackson Merrill** benefits significantly from a favorable clash against Littell (4.63 xERA), where his plate discipline and speed profile are amplified by a positive park factor and a manageable pitching matchup. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned for a breakout performance; his score is heavily bolstered by a robust 14% platoon edge against Canning, making him one of our most reliable engines for both AVG and R/RBI production tonight. While **Gunnar Henderson** (70.51) faces a tougher test against the efficient Miles (2.95 xERA), his elite batted-ball data and a high-leverage spot in the two-hole keep his efficiency comfortably in our \"Strong\" tier.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved balancing **Josh Jung** (58.60) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.23) for the final utility spots. **Josh Jung** ultimately edged out the competition due to superior SP matchup context against Wacha (4.44 xERA) and the stability of the #2 spot in his lineup, whereas **Miguel Vargas** suffered from a slight dip in dynamic platoon efficiency. We are also closely monitoring the injury report, as the continued absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Drake Baldwin** leave our depth thin, necessitating reliance on **Brayan Rocchio** (40.91) despite his current spot at the bottom of the order. Investors should keep a close eye on weather developments, as any shifts in wind patterns could impact the high-ceiling projections for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Andy Pages**, both of whom are projected to thrive in hitter-friendly conditions against their respective opposition.",
